              "summary": "Target tracking adjusts capacity toward a chosen metric target, much like a thermostat regulates temperature. In this example, the target is average CPU utilization of 50%. Increased traffic raises utilization to 75%, and target tracking determines that adding five instances will bring utilization back toward the target. Five instances is the result in this example, not a fixed scaling increment.",
